        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Doc Watson, Charles Carroll of Carrollton\n- Places: Bolton, North Carolina, Homewood Field, Homewood estate\n- Concepts: Birthplaces, eponymous place names, Catholic signatories\n\nFacts:\n- Doc Watson was born in Bolton, North Carolina.\n- Bolton, North Carolina, was named after Charles Carroll of Carrollton.\n- Charles Carroll of Carrollton was the only Catholic signatory to the Declaration of Independence, also known in Irish as Áth an Ghorta.\n- Homewood Field was named for the Homewood estate.\n- The Homewood estate belonged to Charles Carroll of Carrollton.",
